    "description": "As Ops, I want a daily view of deals that failed to sync, so I find out from a report rather than from a rep.\n\n* Report 'Deals — CMS Sync Failed': status in Failed or Retrying, showing deal, external Id, owner, last attempt and note. Saved to a shared Ops folder with a daily subscription to the Ops distribution list\n\n* Report 'Deals — Published but Never Synced': published with no successful sync recorded — catches deals that never achieved a first successful push\n\n* Optional: scheduled alert for deals sitting in Failed beyond a defined threshold (+\\~2h)\n\nEffort: 2-3h. Blocked by BUILD-83.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §4.4.\n\nSCOPE BOUNDARY: covers Salesforce-side errors only — failures of the callout itself up to a non-success HTTP response. Once the CMS acknowledges a payload, Salesforce marks the deal Synced and has no further visibility. Anything the CMS does after acknowledging needs CMS-side monitoring. Same in reverse: Salesforce cannot report on Direction 2 calls that never arrive.",
